===Verb===
{{en-verb|~s|~ing|bought|+,boughten<l:archaic,rare,dialectal>}}

# {{lb|en|transitive|ditransitive}} To [[obtain]] (something) in [[exchange]] for money or goods.
#: {{ux|en|Who'd Father '''buy''' the car for? He '''bought''' it for me, not for you.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1793|author=w:Benjamin Franklin|title={{w|The Autobiography of Benjamin Franklin|Autobiography}}
|passage='''Buy''' what thou hast no need of, and ere long thou wilt sell thy necessaries.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|ditransitive}} To obtain, especially by some sacrifice.
#: {{ux|en|I've '''bought''' material comfort by foregoing my dreams.}}
#: {{ux|en|You just '''bought''' yourself an assault charge!}}
#* {{RQ:KJV|Proverbs|23|23||'''Buy''' the truth and sell it not; also wisdom, and instruction, and understanding.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|archaic}} To [[suffer]] [[consequences]] for (something) through being [[deprive]]d of something; to [[pay]] for (something one has done).
#* {{RQ:Jack Straw|I|15|VVhat villaine, doſt ſtrike me? I ſweare by the rood,<br>As I am ''Iacke Strawe'', thou ſhalt '''buy''' it with thy blood.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[bribe]].
#: {{ux|en|He tried to '''buy''' me with gifts, but I wouldn't give up my beliefs.}}
#* {{quote-web|en|date=20 May 2025|author=Tal Axelrod|work=Axios|title=MAGA faithful grow frustrated with Trump's Justice Department|url=https://www.axios.com/2025/05/20/kash-patel-dan-bongino-epstein-maga-trump|text=After Bongino reiterated that Epstein killed himself, he was flooded with responses of disbelief. "WHO has '''bought''' the both of you?" one X user asked of Bongino and Patel, referencing the Fox News interview.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20260915201731/https://www.axios.com/2025/05/20/kash-patel-dan-bongino-epstein-maga-trump|archivedate=15 September 2026}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To be equivalent to in value.
#: {{ux|en|The dollar doesn't '''buy''' as much as it used to.}}
# {{senseid|en|accept}} {{lb|en|transitive|informal}} to [[accept]] as true; to [[believe]]
#: {{syn|en|swallow|}}
#: {{ux|en|I'm not going to '''buy''' your stupid excuses anymore!}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2020|author=w:Akwaeke Emezi|title=The Death of Vivek Oji|publisher=Faber & Faber Ltd|page=201|passage=People like to say that dead people look asleep, and maybe she would have '''bought''' that under different circumstances.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To make a purchase or purchases, to [[treat]] (for a drink, meal or gift)
#: {{ux|en|She '''buys''' for Federated.}}
#: {{ux|en|Let's go out for dinner. I'm '''buying'''.}}
# {{lb|en|poker slang|transitive}} To make a [[bluff]], usually a large one.
#: {{ux|en|Smith tried to '''buy''' the pot on the river with a huge bluff.}}

